K8S Networking

Deployment -> Replicaset -> Pod
Pods are ephemeral
When a pod gets deleted a new pod will get created.
The created new pod will have different name and different ip.

Since pod ips may change it tough to communicate pod to pod.

ANother object comes into picture which is Kubernetes services.

Kubernetes services (SVC) is an abstraction layer that provides stable network identity.
The svc will sit on top of Kubernetes cluster and the pods communicate through it.
It routes the traffic to the right pods

For each microservice we create one k8s service to send traffic to correct pod.

Types of traffic:
Internal traffic - within k8s pod to pod - service:clusterIP
External traffic - outside traffic - service:NodePort

Create a deployment 
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
	name: nginx-deployment
	labels: 
	   app: nginx
spec:
	replicas: 3
	selector:
	   matchLabels:
		app: nginx
	template:
	   metadata:
		labels:
		   app: nginx
	   spec:
		containers:
		  - name: nginx-container
		    image: nginx:1.25
		    ports:
		      -  containerPort: 80

$ kubectl apply -f nginx-deployment.yaml
$ kubectl get pod
$ kubectl get pod -o wide
$ kubectl delete pod podname
$ kubectl get pod -o wide


$ vi myclusterip.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: nginx-clusterip
  labels: 
    app: nginx
spec:
  selector:
    app: nginx # this much match the Deployment labels
  ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 80 # service port(stable)
      targetPort: 80 # container port inside pod
  type: ClusterIP # default type

$ kubectl apply -f myclusterip.yaml

$ kubbectl get po
$ kubectl get svc
$ kubectl get ep
$ kubectl get ep| grep nginx
$ kubectl get po -o wide
