This is not a good design and true balancing
because we need to use all public ips and port number which exposes ips and port and also we are having one ip for each node not one for all pods also restricted to port range 30000-32767

We have another for this which is available in cloud is loadbalancing

$ kubectl apply -f nginx-deployment.yaml
$ vi mylb.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: nginx-lb
spec:
  type: LoadBalancer
  selector: 
    app: nginx
  ports:
    - port: 80
      targetPort: 80
      protocol: TCP


$ kubectl apply -f mylb.yaml
$ kubectl get svc


$ kubectl delete svc name
$ kubectl delete deploymentname

The loadbalancer is automatically provisioned by cloud provider
